[# docs-src/repos/cx-platform-xap.cxd — the application host's page,
   repo-cx-platform-xap.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 2).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from its own corpus (the
   composition suite). #]

[repo name=cx-platform-xap
  [intro
    """Features compose into an application, and the composition is
       an algebra. `cx-platform-xap` is the host: a feature's grammar — its
       nouns, verbs and requirements — is a data document, two features
       compose into one grammar whichever order you name them in, and the
       host serves the composed grammar to a terminal, a browser and an agent
       through one cascade."""]
  [body
    """Every intent commits through one synchronous, journal-folded path: the
       bus calls the policy decision once, appends to the hash-chained
       journal and re-folds state, and a rejected intent is a value on the
       failure channel rather than a crash. Reads are a deterministic fold
       over the log. Agents are peers — they emit the same intents a human
       client does, gated by the same authorization dial."""]
  [body
    """The [XAP overview](xap.html) and its four demo pages are the ladder:
       one capability, surfaced through progressively more clients, each rung
       turning on exactly one more subsystem, every page embedding the demo's
       real source and its recorded output. Sealing, publishing and
       installing a feature is [[xap-distribution]]; the platform chapter of
       the primer is projected from this repository's composition and
       deployment-topology pages."""]
  [gives
    """The module below is the runtime a program imports. Beside it the
       registry carries this repository's three conformance suites —
       composition, schema-as-data and the `on` handler surface — and the
       distribution natives; the corpus link at the foot of the page holds
       them all."""]
  [try
    """Two features composed. Each declares a `highlight` verb of its own;
       composition keeps both, because a verb is qualified by the feature
       that declares it — four verbs in the composed grammar, none lost, none
       renamed."""]
  [fixture id=xap-compose-006-same-named-verbs-coexist]
  [status
    """The host builds on the widest set of platform repositories on this
       site — the wire, mail, identity, the store, the database drivers, the
       fabric and the session layer — and the figure draws every one of them
       from the registry's own row."""]]
